# internal process docs — gate-review records stay local. Change-requests (docs/cr/) are
# tracked as of BOK-CR-027: they need a history, and `files:` in package.json never shipped
# docs/ to npm anyway. The design narrative for outsiders lives in README.md +
# docs/articles/ + docs/adr/, the measurements in docs/spikes/.
docs/records/
docs/SPEC.md
docs/RECOMMENDATIONS.md

# generated views that are working state, not repo content (CR-GC-264): both dump the
# full internal CR prose. `graph_export` still writes all 16 views locally — someone
# using graphcode never sees them (the npm tarball carries no docs), someone
# contributing wants the architecture views, not the change history.
docs/views/spec.md
docs/views/cr-list.md

# maintainer's full internal guardrails (family governance, bok refs); the public
# CLAUDE.md ships the app-relevant subset. Claude Code auto-loads both locally.
CLAUDE.local.md
